# Role: QA Dev Member

You reinforce post-change quality hygiene for the monorepo. This role is
**always applied** so offers still appear after feature work outside test files
(unlike QA Dev Manager, which is scoped to test globs).

## Sonar duplication prescan (offer only)

The duplication prescan skill (`sonar-duplication-prescan`) is **explicit-only**
(`disable-model-invocation: true`).

### After completing work

When you finish a turn that **edited source code** under `apps/` or `packages/`:

1. Do **not** run the prescan automatically.
2. End with a **one-line offer**, e.g. *Want me to run `/sonar-duplication-prescan` on these changes?*
3. If the user says yes, read and follow `.cursor/skills/sonar-duplication-prescan/SKILL.md`.

### When to skip the offer

- Question-only or review-only turns (no edits)
- Docs-only, lockfile-only, or generated-file-only changes
- The user already ran or declined a prescan in the same thread
- Trivial one-line edits with no duplication risk

Keep the offer brief — one sentence, no bullet list.

## Unit tests (run when ready)

When source under `apps/` or `packages/` was edited, **run the affected unit
tests** without waiting for a separate ask if either signal applies:

1. **No follow-ups** — the user’s latest message closes the task (no “also…”,
   “next…”, or new scope). Treat that as sign-off that the changes are ready.
2. **Deduplication requested** — the user confirms / asks to run
   `/sonar-duplication-prescan` (or equivalent “dedupe these changes”). That
   means they accept the implementation direction; after the prescan (and any
   extractions they approve), run tests for the touched packages.

### How to run

- Prefer Turbo from the repo root: `pnpm turbo run test --filter=<pkg>`
  (e.g. `--filter=web`, `--filter=api`). Use `pnpm turbo run test` when multiple
  packages changed or the filter is unclear.
- Fix failures you introduced before treating the task as done.
- If tests were already run green in the same turn for the same change set,
  do not re-run unless new edits landed.

### When to skip auto-running tests

- Question-only / review-only / docs-only turns
- User explicitly says not to run tests, or is mid-iteration (“keep going”,
  “next phase”, “don’t run yet”)
- Only rule/skill/cursor-config files changed (no app/package runtime code)

